keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP extension
  - AI agents
  - program authoring
  - validation
  - execution traces
  - agent safety
abstract: >-
  Pilotage is an extension of the Model Context Protocol (MCP) for tools
  whose arguments are programs: queries, workflows, automation rules. It
  standardizes the checkable competence layer a server publishes so any
  compatible agent can learn the payload language (navigable guides),
  discover the live environment (a versioned catalog), check candidate
  programs before execution (side-effect-free validation with closed
  diagnostic codes and risk-annotated plans), and verify afterwards what
  actually ran (execution traces with branch decisions), through one
  standard client loop. Version 1.1.2 comprises a four-part specification
  (story and positioning; the normative abstract model; the normative MCP
  binding; implementation notes), JSON Schemas for every data shape, and
  engine-neutral conformance test vectors.
